# VHS tape template for the README's CLI tour (https://github.com/charmbracelet/vhs).
#
# Not runnable as-is: the __FEED_ID__ / __WATCH_ID__ / __ACTION_ID__ / __RUN_ID__
# placeholders are the ids of a seeded watch on YOUR running stack, so they are
# resolved at record time. Render + record with scripts/demo/cli-record.sh,
# never with `vhs` directly on this file.
#
# __PAGER__ marks where the `activity list` pager prompt is answered. The CLI
# prompt-pages on a TTY (which a VHS shell is) whenever a next page exists, so
# the renderer swaps the marker for a `Type "n"` answer when one will, and
# drops it when one won't; either way the next narration line lands in the
# shell, not the prompt.
#
# The narrative is the post-quickstart tour, in pipeline order: feeds (your
# sources), the watch and its semantic filter (what reads them), then the
# activity log (what matched, with scores and links). Every id a command takes
# is on screen first, in the table of the `list` that precedes it, so the tour
# reads as something the viewer could retype. The typed `#` lines are on-screen
# narration; bash ignores them.

Output assets/cli-tour.gif

Require magpie

Set Shell bash
Set FontSize 15
Set Width 1500
Set Height 800
Set Padding 16
Set TypingSpeed 30ms
Set Theme "Catppuccin Mocha"

Type "# Welcome to the magpie CLI"
Enter
Sleep 1.5s

Type "# A feed is a set of sources polled for new posts"
Enter
Sleep 1.5s
Type "magpie feed list"
Enter
Sleep 3s
Type "magpie feed get __FEED_ID__"
Enter
Sleep 4s

Type "# A watch reads its feeds through a chain of actions"
Enter
Sleep 1.5s
Type "magpie watch list"
Enter
Sleep 3s
Type "magpie watch action list --watch __WATCH_ID__"
Enter
Sleep 4s

Type "# The semantic filter: what to look for in plain language, plus the minimum score to match"
Enter
Sleep 2.5s
Type "magpie watch action get __ACTION_ID__"
Enter
Sleep 5s

Type "# Your LLM scores each new post against those instructions. These cleared the bar:"
Enter
Sleep 1.5s
Type "magpie activity list --action __ACTION_ID__ --state succeeded --limit 5 --columns run.id,run.result.score,feed_item.title,feed_item.url"
Enter
Sleep 5s
__PAGER__

Type "# One match in full: the source link, the score, and why the model said yes"
Enter
Sleep 1.5s
Type "magpie activity get __RUN_ID__"
Enter
Sleep 10s
